  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Adjust oven rack to middle position and preheat oven to 425°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. In a small bowl, whisk together cream cheese, sugar, and salt until smooth; set aside. In a separate small bowl, whisk together egg with 1 teaspoon water.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Lightly flour a clean work surface. Roll 1/2 of puff pastry into a 11 by 9 1/2-inch rectangle, positioning it so that the shorter side is at the top of your workspace. Cut rectangle into 3 equal vertical columns. Cover the bottom half of each rectangle with about 1 heaping tablespoon of the cream cheese mixture and cover with raspberries. Fold dough over to form a pocket and use your fingers to crimp and seal the sides of the dough. Slash horizontal lines across top of dough, 1/2-inch apart. Use your fingers to gently open cuts until filling peeks through. Brush each rectangle with egg wash and place on baking sheet. Repeat process with remaining dough.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "Bake pastries until golden, about 20 minutes. Transfer to a wire rack to cool slightly. Serve warm.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
